{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01DhvsEodZ6Ehg2njZQkJ9PK", "type": "tool_result", "content": "Web search results for query: \"TinyStories\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"TinyStories: How Small Can Language Models Be and Still Speak Coherent English?\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2305.07759\"},{\"title\":\"hyper.ai\",\"url\":\"https://hyper.ai/en/datasets/33032\"},{\"title\":\"www.huggingface.co\",\"url\":\"https://www.huggingface.co/datasets/roneneldan/TinyStories/blob/main/README.md?code=true\"},{\"title\":\"huggingface.co\",\"url\":\"https://huggingface.co/datasets/roneneldan/TinyStories\"},{\"title\":\"Multilingual TinyStories: A Synthetic Combinatorial Corpus of Indic Children's Stories for Training Small Language Models\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2603.14563\"},{\"title\":\"TinyStories: How Small Can Language Models Be and Still Speak Coherent English?\",\"url\":\"https://deepai.org/publication/tinystories-how-small-can-language-models-be-and-still-speak-coherent-english\"},{\"title\":\"TinyStories: How Small Can Language Models Be and Still Speak Coherent English?\",\"url\":\"https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/research/?p=973236\"},{\"title\":\"Loading Events\",\"url\":\"https://www.math.harvard.edu/event/the-tinystories-dataset-how-small-can-language-models-be-and-still-speak-coherent-english/\"},{\"title\":\"Loading Events\",\"url\":\"https://cmsa.fas.harvard.edu/event/nt-92023\"},{\"title\":\"TinyStories: How Small Can Language Models Be and Still Speak Coherent\\\\n English?\",\"url\":\"https://liner.com/ko/review/tinystories-how-small-can-language-models-be-and-still-speak\"},{\"title\":\"tinystories small language models that still speak coherent\",\"url\":\"https://www.alignmentforum.[scrubbed:long-base64]\"},{\"title\":\"Quick review\",\"url\":\"https://liner.com/review/tinystories-how-small-can-language-models-be-and-still-speak\"},{\"title\":\"tinystories 4ce620e569a4\",\"url\":\"https://cobusgreyling.medium.com/tinystories-4ce620e569a4\"},{\"title\":\"hyper.ai\",\"url\":\"https://hyper.ai/cn/datasets/33032\"},{\"title\":\"The Tiny Model Revolution with Ronen Eldan and Yuanzhi Li of Microsoft Research\",\"url\":\"https://cognitiverevolution.ai/the-tiny-model-revolution-with-ronen-eldan-and-yuanzhi-li-of-microsoft-research\"},{\"title\":\"Source code for oumi.datasets.pretraining.tiny_stories\",\"url\":\"https://oumi.ai/docs/en/latest/_modules/oumi/datasets/pretraining/tiny_stories.html\"},{\"title\":\"www.alphaxiv.org\",\"url\":\"https://www.alphaxiv.org/overview/2504.09184\"},{\"title\":\"🚀NEW COURSEVibe Coding AI Apps with Claude Code 🤖✨Enroll now\",\"url\":\"https://academy.dair.ai/papers/tinystories\"},{\"title\":\"Go backThe blogThis article\",\"url\":\"https://sfcompute.com/blog/tiny-narrations\"},{\"title\":\"meilu.jpshuntong.com\",\"url\":\"https://meilu.jpshuntong.com/url-68747470733a2f2f61727869762e6f7267/pdf/2305.07759.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"www.wizwand.com\",\"url\":\"https://www.wizwand.com/dataset/tinystories\"}]\n\nTinyStories is a synthetic dataset of short stories from Microsoft Research, created to train and study small language models.\n\n- **Origin and purpose:** Microsoft Research proposed it in 2023 in the paper \"TinyStories: How Small Can Language Models Be and Still Speak Coherent English?\" by Ronen Eldan and Yuanzhi Li. The authors built it to train small models, under 10 million parameters, that can produce fluent, consistent narratives (TinyStories, a synthetic dataset of short stories for training and evaluating SLMs (below 10 million parameters) to produce fluent and consistent narratives.).\n- **Content:** The stories were generated by GPT-3.5 and GPT-4 and use vocabulary a typical 3- to 4-year-old would understand (a synthetic dataset of short stories that only contain words that a typical 3 to 4-year-olds usually understand).\n- **Versions:** The original set mixes GPT-3.5 and GPT-4 output. A later release, TinyStoriesV2-GPT4, uses only GPT-4 generations, which are of higher quality (based on generations by GPT-4 only (the original dataset also has generations by GPT-3.5 which are of lesser quality)).\n- **Availability:** It is on Hugging Face as roneneldan/TinyStories. One source notes it is released under the CDLA-Sharing-1.0 license.\n- **Criticism and successors:** A later ETH Zürich-led project, SimpleStories, was built to improve on it. It reports that 59% of TinyStories samples began with the formulaic phrase \"Once upon a time,\" creating a highly repetitive dataset.\n- **Derivatives:** Other projects have built on it, including a Multilingual TinyStories corpus covering 17 Indian languages and a synthetic audio dataset released by SF Compute.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "8b1a8918-c965-42c5-8b95-f6cb2b44aa09", "uuid": "13a36276-bd82-420f-8230-5c6ff8a66f1b", "timestamp": "2026-11-02T20:15:11.773Z", "tool_use_result": {"query": "TinyStories", "results": [{"tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_018VaJW2vxTBKKqaraZ81WfF", "content": [{"title": "TinyStories: How Small Can Language Models Be and Still Speak Coherent English?", "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2305.07759"}, {"title": "hyper.ai", "url": "https://hyper.ai/en/datasets/33032"}, {"title": "www.huggingface.co", "url": "https://www.huggingface.co/datasets/roneneldan/TinyStories/blob/main/README.md?code=true"}, {"title": "huggingface.co", "url": "https://huggingface.co/datasets/roneneldan/TinyStories"}, {"title": "Multilingual TinyStories: A Synthetic Combinatorial Corpus of Indic Children's Stories for Training Small Language Models", "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2603.14563"}, {"title": "TinyStories: How Small Can Language Models Be and Still Speak Coherent English?", "url": "https://deepai.org/publication/tinystories-how-small-can-language-models-be-and-still-speak-coherent-english"}, {"title": "TinyStories: How Small Can Language Models Be and Still Speak Coherent English?", "url": "https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/research/?p=973236"}, {"title": "Loading Events", "url": "https://www.math.harvard.edu/event/the-tinystories-dataset-how-small-can-language-models-be-and-still-speak-coherent-english/"}, {"title": "Loading Events", "url": "https://cmsa.fas.harvard.edu/event/nt-92023"}, {"title": "TinyStories: How Small Can Language Models Be and Still Speak Coherent\\n English?", "url": "https://liner.com/ko/review/tinystories-how-small-can-language-models-be-and-still-speak"}, {"title": "tinystories small language models that still speak coherent", "url": "https://www.alignmentforum.[scrubbed:long-base64]"}, {"title": "Quick review", "url": "https://liner.com/review/tinystories-how-small-can-language-models-be-and-still-speak"}, {"title": "tinystories 4ce620e569a4", "url": "https://cobusgreyling.medium.com/tinystories-4ce620e569a4"}, {"title": "hyper.ai", "url": "https://hyper.ai/cn/datasets/33032"}, {"title": "The Tiny Model Revolution with Ronen Eldan and Yuanzhi Li of Microsoft Research", "url": "https://cognitiverevolution.ai/the-tiny-model-revolution-with-ronen-eldan-and-yuanzhi-li-of-microsoft-research"}, {"title": "Source code for oumi.datasets.pretraining.tiny_stories", "url": "https://oumi.ai/docs/en/latest/_modules/oumi/datasets/pretraining/tiny_stories.html"}, {"title": "www.alphaxiv.org", "url": "https://www.alphaxiv.org/overview/2504.09184"}, {"title": "🚀NEW COURSEVibe Coding AI Apps with Claude Code 🤖✨Enroll now", "url": "https://academy.dair.ai/papers/tinystories"}, {"title": "Go backThe blogThis article", "url": "https://sfcompute.com/blog/tiny-narrations"}, {"title": "meilu.jpshuntong.com", "url": "https://meilu.jpshuntong.com/url-68747470733a2f2f61727869762e6f7267/pdf/2305.07759.pdf"}, {"title": "www.wizwand.com", "url": "https://www.wizwand.com/dataset/tinystories"}]}, "TinyStories is a synthetic dataset of short stories from Microsoft Research, created to train and study small language models.\n\n- **Origin and purpose:** Microsoft Research proposed it in 2023 in the paper \"TinyStories: How Small Can Language Models Be and Still Speak Coherent English?\" by Ronen Eldan and Yuanzhi Li. The authors built it to train small models, under 10 million parameters, that can produce fluent, consistent narratives (TinyStories, a synthetic dataset of short stories for training and evaluating SLMs (below 10 million parameters) to produce fluent and consistent narratives.).\n- **Content:** The stories were generated by GPT-3.5 and GPT-4 and use vocabulary a typical 3- to 4-year-old would understand (a synthetic dataset of short stories that only contain words that a typical 3 to 4-year-olds usually understand).\n- **Versions:** The original set mixes GPT-3.5 and GPT-4 output. A later release, TinyStoriesV2-GPT4, uses only GPT-4 generations, which are of higher quality (based on generations by GPT-4 only (the original dataset also has generations by GPT-3.5 which are of lesser quality)).\n- **Availability:** It is on Hugging Face as roneneldan/TinyStories. One source notes it is released under the CDLA-Sharing-1.0 license.\n- **Criticism and successors:** A later ETH Zürich-led project, SimpleStories, was built to improve on it. It reports that 59% of TinyStories samples began with the formulaic phrase \"Once upon a time,\" creating a highly repetitive dataset.\n- **Derivatives:** Other projects have built on it, including a Multilingual TinyStories corpus covering 17 Indian languages and a synthetic audio dataset released by SF Compute."], "durationSeconds": 5.461676118000003, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01DhvsEodZ6Ehg2njZQkJ9PK", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "config", "reason_type": "rule"}}]}
